---
import CapabilityList from "./CapabilityList.astro";
import SectionHeading from "./SectionHeading.astro";

interface Props {
  number: string;
}

const { number } = Astro.props;
---

<section class="section wrap" aria-labelledby="about">
  <SectionHeading id="about" number={number} title="About" />

  <div class="grid">
    <div class="text">
      <p class="lead">
        I am a full-stack software developer. I take a problem from its first
        requirement to tested, shipped software, with web applications in
        TypeScript, React and Next.js on PostgreSQL backends where access
        control and data integrity are treated as requirements, not
        afterthoughts.
      </p>
      <p>
        My MSc in Advanced Computer Science at the University of Exeter ended in
        a dissertation on large language models: I designed and ran a study of
        how far prompt design can control text simplification, evaluated with
        readability and semantic-similarity metrics and paired statistics.
      </p>
      <p>
        I have also worked as a content creator and video editor, and I founded
        and ran a small student-focused business. Both taught me to work for an
        audience, communicate clearly and own an outcome from start to finish.
      </p>

      <h3 class="label">How I work</h3>
      <ul class="style">
        <li>I clarify the requirement before writing the solution.</li>
        <li>I keep a written decision log.</li>
        <li>I test at database level, not just in the UI.</li>
        <li>
          I use modern development tooling and review and test every change.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <CapabilityList />
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 3rem;
  }

  .text {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .text > p + p {
    margin-top: 1.1rem;
  }

  .lead {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: clamp(1.125rem, 1.02rem + 0.45vw, 1.3125rem);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  h3 {
    margin-top: 2.25rem;
  }

  .style {
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .style li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
  }

  .style li + li {
    margin-top: 0.4rem;
  }

  .style li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.8em;
    width: 0.5rem;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--accent);
  }

  @media (min-width: 64rem) {
    .grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.15fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 4.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
